// Literal flexing is bounded by the target type: a literal that does not fit
// is a compile error, not a silent wrap. The message names the offending value;
// the span covers the whole `if`, since that is the expression being flexed to
// the declared `u8` return.
fn f(b: bool) -> u8 { if (b) { 1 } else { 300 } }

fn main() {}
--- errors ---
error: integer literal 300 does not fit in u8
 --> ./tests/cases/integers/errors/err_literal_too_big.aipl:5:27
  |
5 | fn f(b: bool) -> u8 { if (b) { 1 } else { 300 } }
  |                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
